<title>USA: U.S. FY 1996 budget deficit $107.3 billion.</title>
<headline>U.S. FY 1996 budget deficit $107.3 billion.</headline>
<dateline>ST.LOUIS 1996-10-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The White House said on Monday that the fiscal year 1996 budget deficit was $107.3 billion versus 1995's $163.9 billion.</p>
<p>The White House said in a document released in St. Louis, where President Clinton is campaigning, that the budget deficit was the smallest since 1981.</p>
<p>It said the deficit represented 1.4 percent of gross domestic product, the smallest deficit as a share of GDP since 1974.</p>
</text>
